#: src/languages/rego.md:3
msgid "Rego"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:5
msgid ""
"Rego language support in Zed is provided by the community-maintained [Rego "
"extension](https://github.com/StyraInc/zed-rego)."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:7
msgid ""
"Tree-sitter: [FallenAngel97/tree-sitter-rego](https://github.com/"
"FallenAngel97/tree-sitter-rego)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:8
msgid ""
"Language Server: [open-policy-agent/regal](https://github.com/open-policy-"
"agent/regal)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:10
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:12
msgid ""
"The extension is largely based on the [Regal](https://docs.styra.com/regal/"
"language-server) language server which should be installed to make use of "
"the extension. Read the [getting started](https://docs.styra.com/"
"regal#getting-started) instructions for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:14
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:16
msgid ""
"The extension's behavior is configured in the `.regal/config.yaml` file. The "
"following is an example configuration which disables the `todo-comment` "
"rule, customizes the `line-length` rule, and ignores test files for the `opa-"
"fmt` rule:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:19
msgid "rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:20
msgid "style"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:21
msgid "todo-comment"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:22
msgid ""
"# don't report on todo comments\n"
"      level"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:23
msgid "ignore"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:24
msgid "line-length"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:25
msgid ""
"# custom rule configuration\n"
"      max-line-length"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:27
msgid ""
"# warn on too long lines, but don't fail\n"
"      level"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:28
msgid "warning"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:29
msgid "opa-fmt"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:30
msgid ""
"# not needed as error is the default, but\n"
"      # being explicit won't hurt\n"
"      level"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:32
msgid "error"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:33
msgid ""
"# files can be ignored for any individual rule\n"
"      # in this example, test files are ignored\n"
"      ignore"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:36
msgid "files"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:37
msgid "\"*_test.rego\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/rego.md:40
msgid ""
"Read Regal's [configuration documentation](https://docs.styra.com/"
"regal#configuration) for more information."
msgstr ""
